\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 1. Interpretation: Style, Biases, Triggers, and Risk Points\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 The overall shape.
\f0\b0 \strokec2  Narcissism, Machiavellianism, psychopathy, and sadism are sometimes grouped in psychology as the "Dark Tetrad" \'97 shorthand for traits that, at high levels, can undermine relationships and trust. In your profile, three of the four sit at or below the midpoint; none are elevated. Machiavellianism is the exception: modestly above the midpoint, and the highest of your four dark-trait scores. Meanwhile, all three positive-leadership traits are comfortably above the midpoint, with humility especially high.\
Together, this reads as a 
\f1\b \strokec2 pragmatic, ethically-anchored style
\f0\b0 \strokec2 : someone who thinks strategically about influence, timing, and framing, but with strong internal guardrails \'97 humility and ethical leadership \'97 that keep the strategic instinct from tipping into manipulation. Empathy adds a genuine relational layer on top.\

\f1\b \strokec2 Biases worth watching
\f0\b0 \strokec2 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\i \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Motive-reading
\f0\i0 : moderate Machiavellianism tends to come with a slightly more cynical read of others' motives \'97 an assumption that people are also playing an angle. This can lead to over-interpreting ordinary behavior as political maneuvering.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\i \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 "Whatever works" pull
\f0\i0 : under pressure, this trait can nudge decisions toward what's effective over what's most transparent, even when you wouldn't consciously choose that trade-off.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\i \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The shadow side of very high humility
\f0\i0 : at 82, humility is your greatest asset \'97 but taken far enough, it can also tip into underselling your own contributions or hesitating to assert a strong position when a moment calls for confident, visible leadership.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Workplace triggers
\f0\b0 \strokec2  \'97 situations more likely to pull you toward the less helpful end of this profile:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Competitive moments: credit disputes, promotion cycles, resource allocation.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Being publicly challenged or having your judgment questioned in front of others.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 High-pressure moments (deadlines, crises, layoffs) where empathy has to compete with strategic thinking for the same bandwidth.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Conflict or underperformance conversations, where the pull may be toward controlling the narrative rather than a more transparent, collaborative process.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Overall risk level
\f0\b0 \strokec2 : modest and specific, not acute. With psychopathy and sadism this low, this isn't a profile associated with callousness or a taste for others' discomfort. The real risk is narrower \'97 a gap that can open, especially under stress, between how strategic you're actually being and how transparent people expect you to be.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 2. Top 3 Risks to Monitor\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 1. Strategic opacity that erodes trust.
\f0\b0 \strokec2  Machiavellianism's main workplace expression is managing information and framing more than colleagues realize \'97 sharing on a need-to-know basis, or shaping a message to manage perception rather than stating full reasoning. Any one instance is minor; the risk compounds if it becomes a pattern people notice and start discounting your directness for.\

\f1\b \strokec2 2. Status sensitivity under challenge.
\f0\b0 \strokec2  Moderate narcissism (46) usually just means ordinary, healthy self-regard \'97 but under public criticism or being overlooked, that can tip into defensiveness or subtly steering the conversation back to your own framing.\

\f1\b \strokec2 3. Empathy dropping out under load.
\f0\b0 \strokec2  Empathy (64) is real, but it competes for the same mental bandwidth as strategic thinking \'97 bandwidth that shrinks under stress. The risk is that your default shifts to "efficient and strategic" and away from "curious and relational" exactly when people most need to feel heard: tight deadlines, conflict, hard news.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 3. Top 3 Strengths \'97 and How They Offset the Risks\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 1. High humility (82) \'97 your strongest asset.
\f0\b0 \strokec2  This predicts genuine openness to feedback and a fast willingness to admit and correct mistakes. It directly offsets Risk #2: even if a defensive flash shows up, humility creates a quick self-correction loop instead of letting ego dig in.\

\f1\b \strokec2 2. Strong ethical leadership (79).
\f0\b0 \strokec2  This is your values-based check on the Machiavellian streak \'97 a clear internal line for where "strategic" tips into "misleading." It offsets Risk #1 by flagging, usually before you act, when managing a message starts to cross into managing the truth.\

\f1\b \strokec2 3. Above-average empathy (64).
\f0\b0 \strokec2  Because this is a real, practiced skill rather than something to build from scratch, it's a strength you can deliberately lean on. It offsets Risk #3 if you treat high-stress moments as the specific cue to consciously over-invest in it, rather than assuming it'll show up on its own.\

\f1\b \strokec2 Why the combination matters.
\f0\b0 \strokec2  Moderate Machiavellianism paired with high ethical leadership and high humility is a genuinely favorable pattern. It tends to produce someone who can navigate politics and stakeholders skillfully without crossing into manipulation, because the values-based traits act as guardrails on the strategic instinct.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 4. A 2\'964 Week Improvement Plan\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 Built as four one-week blocks. Short on time? Run Weeks 1\'962 \'97 they target your two clearest risk areas. Weeks 3\'964 extend the work into empathy-under-load and integration.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 \strokec2 Week 1 \'97 Transparency
\f0\b0 \strokec2  
\f2\i \strokec2 (targets Risk #1)
\f0\i0 \strokec2 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Micro-experiment
\f0\b0 : In two meetings this week, proactively share one piece of context or reasoning you'd normally only reveal if asked.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Reflection questions
\f0\b0 : Where did I hold information back this week \'97 for a legitimate reason (confidentiality, timing), or a strategic one (managing perception)? Did more transparency cost me anything, or build something?\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Workplace behaviour
\f0\b0 : Before sending a carefully-worded message, ask: "Would I be comfortable if the recipient saw my unedited reasoning?" If not, take a second look.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Week 2 \'97 Feedback and status-sensitivity
\f0\b0 \strokec2  
\f2\i \strokec2 (targets Risk #2, builds on humility)
\f0\i0 \strokec2 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
